P-5 fix 1, S2: window-to-window CopyArea copies only what of the source is
visible and reports the rest (build-tree patch against isoriano1968/x11r6.3-amix
cb61a21, applied after zz9000hw-modes.patch and p5-1-solidrect-alu.patch).

ZZ9000CopyArea copied the whole source rectangle out of the framebuffer, so
where the source window was covered it copied the covering window's pixels,
and it returned NULL, so no GraphicsExpose was ever sent.  Now, as in
cfbBitBlt: the source rectangle is clipped to the source window's clipList
(NotClippedByChildren for IncludeInferiors), translated to the destination
and clipped to the composite clip; only that region is copied, bands and
boxes in an overlap-safe order; miHandleExposures paints the destination
background over the uncopyable part and returns the exposed region.

Proof: x11/bench/copyexpose (both cases FAIL on 709b8a97, the rig,
2026-09-27); the box order is checked host-side by x11/bench/copyarea-order.c.

--- a/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/zz9000/zz9000draw.c
+++ b/programs/Xserver/hw/amix/rtg/zz9000/zz9000draw.c
@@ -635,12 +635,18 @@
 ** ZZ9000CopyArea - copy a rectangular region between drawables.
 **
 ** Fast path: both drawables are windows on the same screen -> direct VRAM
-** copy clipped against the GC composite clip.
+** copy.  Modelled on cfbBitBlt: the source rectangle is first clipped to
+** what of the source window is actually visible (its clipList, or the
+** area not clipped by children for IncludeInferiors), translated to the
+** destination and clipped to the GC composite clip.  Only that region is
+** copied -- the framebuffer under an obscured part of the source holds
+** some other window's pixels, not the source's.  miHandleExposures then
+** paints the destination background over the parts that could not be
+** copied and, with graphics exposures on, returns the region the client
+** must redraw (the GraphicsExpose events).
 **
 ** All other cases (pixmap source or destination) fall back to miCopyArea,
 ** which uses GetSpans/SetSpans (correct but slower).
-**
-** Returns NULL (no backing-store damage region).
 */
 RegionPtr
 ZZ9000CopyArea(pSrcDraw, pDstDraw, pGC, srcx, srcy, width, height, dstx, dsty)
@@ -651,18 +657,17 @@
